<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills 18 pct sold, yield 17.34 pct.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills 18 pct sold, yield 17.34 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bulgarian Finance Ministry's offer of 20 billion levs of four-week discount T-bills was 17.69 percent sold on Monday, yielding 17.34 percent until maturity, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices are in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		     BG3010697004</p>
<p> Par value			  20 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date		     January 13, 1997</p>
<p> Issue date			 January 15, 1997</p>
<p> Maturity date		    February 12, 1997</p>
<p> Bids received		    3.653 bln levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids		85.17 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		    3.537 bln levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	     85.22 pct</p>
<p> Average yield to maturity    17.34 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
